* Copy operations -- where to start

  OK, so we've got copy constructors for OpBox and OpDesk,
  and a ^C/^V operation in OpDesk triggers the copy operations
  just fine.

  But when we derive classes like MyBox and MyButton, it gets
  tricky what those copy constructors should do. eg. MyBox's
  copy constructor needs to tell OpBox to make a dupe:

  	MyBox::MyBox(const MyBox &o) : OpBox(o) {
	}

  The problem here is the OpBox(o) copy ctor is going to try
  to create copies of OpButtons, instead of MyButtons.

  Seems like we need a way to take over the OpBox copy constructor
  somehow, so that we can create MyButton instances, instead of
  letting OpBox create OpButton instances. eg:

      OpBox                      MyBox         
      -------------------        -------------------------------------- 
     :   -------------   |      |                                      |
     :  | OpButton    |  |      |   OpBox                              |
     :   -------------   |      |   --------------------------------   |
     :   -------------   |      |  |                                |  |
     :  | OpButton    |  |      |  |    MyButton                    |  |
     :   -------------   |      |  |    ------------------------    |  |
     :___________________|      |  |   |   --------------       |   |  |
                                |  |   |  | OpButton     |      |   |  |
				|  |   |   --------------       |   |  |
                                |  |    ------------------------    |  |
                                |  |                                |  |
                                |  |    MyButton                    |  |
                                |  |    ------------------------    |  |
                                |  |   |   --------------       |   |  |
                                |  |   |  | OpButton     |      |   |  |
                                |  |   |   --------------       |   |  |
                                |  |    ------------------------    |  |
                                |  |                                |  |

   Maybe OpBox's copy constructor should call a virtual method CopyButtons()
   to handle copying the OpButtons, so that MyBox can override it to make
   copies of 'MyButtons' instead.

* Make copy constructors for OpButton, OpBox, OpConnect
  so that groups of boxes can be copied.



